    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n28309" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mĕdĭātor</span></b> ,
			ōris, m.
		medius, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a mediator</i> (post-class., esp. in eccl. Lat.): 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">tot mediatorum praesentia,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">App. M. 9, 36, p. 202</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mediator unius non est,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gal. 3, 20</span></i>
			; cf. v. 19; <i><span class="en">id. Heb. 8, 6</span></i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">mediator advenit, id est Deus in carne,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Lact. 4, 25</span></i>
			; <i><span class="en">Tert. Carn. 15</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">id. Resurr. 51 al.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Aug. Conf. 10, 42, 2 sq.</span></i></div>
